    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions on the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so responders can identify the correct access point without delay, as the property has only one way in and out.\n• Trim vegetation along the curved driveway so that oncoming vehicles and pedestrians are visible around bends.\n• Keep the driveway clear of parked vehicles so that fire apparatus and ambulances can reach the main residence and detached structure without obstruction.\n• Post a visible marker or sign at the detached structure identifying it as a separate building on the property.\n• Keep a gate or pathway to the rear of the property unlocked and clearly marked so responders can reach it without searching.\n• Trim shrubs or trees that overhang or narrow the driveway to maintain clearance for large emergency vehicles.\n• If a gate controls driveway access, equip it with a Knox Box or compatible emergency access lock so responders are not delayed at the entrance."
